(a) All proposed actions, ventures, or enterprises which may pose an adverse impact on the quality of the environment shall obtain an environmental permit from the county prior to beginning operations or development.
(b) Environmental permits shall be required for the following proposed or planned actions:
(1) Industrial operations which produce smoke, vapors or odors;
(2) Industrial operations which handle, store toxic materials or produce toxic waste;
(3) Ventures which involve salvage or recycling operations;
(4) Solid waste disposal operations;
(5) Solid waste transfer stations/operations;
(6) Inert landfills; and
(7) Other proposed actions covered by subsection (a) of this section.
(Ord. of 2-5-2002, art. II)
